config HALO_SFXR_ASYNC_THREAD_STACK_SIZE
	int "Async SFXR thread stack size"
	default 2048
	depends on HALO_LUA_SOUND
	help
	  Stack size for the frame.sound.play_async worker thread.

config HALO_SFXR_ASYNC_THREAD_PRIORITY
	int "Async SFXR thread priority"
	default 6
	range 0 15
	depends on HALO_LUA_SOUND
	help
	  Priority for asynchronous frame.sound playback. Lower number is higher
	  priority. Must be higher priority (lower number) than the Lua REPL
	  thread (HALO_LUA_REPL_TASK_PRIORITY): a busy Lua loop would otherwise
	  starve the worker and queued sounds - including the button hold cues -
	  never play. The worker spends nearly all its time blocked on I2S
	  writes, so the high priority costs little.

